flowchart TB
    accTitle: Global and scoped file selection have different boundaries
    accDescr: The observed comparison retains every observed file. Global forceInclude, includeOnly, and exclude determine the globally eligible population. Each named scope begins only from that population, applies a hard includeOnly boundary, and may use local forceInclude only against local exclusions. A globally excluded lockfile remains observed but cannot be reintroduced by its scope.

    observed("Observed comparison retains every observed file"):::focus
    global("Global selection: forceInclude, then includeOnly, then exclude")
    eligible("Globally eligible files"):::ok
    scope("Every named scope starts only from globally eligible files")
    boundary("Scope includeOnly is a hard boundary; local forceInclude overrides only a local exclusion")
    selected("Selected scope members"):::ok
    overlap("Scopes may overlap; they are not partitions")

    lockfile("Observed lockfile: package-lock.json"):::bad
    empty("Global exclusion makes the lockfiles scope exactly empty for this complete input"):::bad

    observed --> global
    global --> eligible
    eligible --> scope
    scope --> boundary
    boundary --> selected
    selected --> overlap

    observed --> lockfile
    lockfile --> empty
